/**
 * @defgroup Foundation_Workflows_Build Build
 * @ingroup Foundation_Workflows_Development
 * @brief Configure a preset and compile one or more targets.
 *
 * The build workflow first configures the selected preset, then invokes CMake
 * using `build/<preset>` as the binary directory. It therefore works even when
 * a configure preset has no matching build preset.
 * Calling build repeatedly is incremental unless `--clean-first`, `-CleanFirst`,
 * or a fresh/clean operation invalidates prior outputs.
 *
 * @section FoundationWorkflowBuildBash Bash
 *
 * @code{bash}
 * ./scripts/build.sh <preset> [--config <name>] [--target <name>] \
 *     [--parallel <jobs>] [--clean-first] [--fresh] [--examples-on]
 *
 * ./scripts/build.sh macos_arm64 --config Release --parallel 8
 * ./scripts/build.sh macos_arm64 --config Debug --target Foundation --clean-first
 * ./scripts/build.sh stm32f407_armgcc_cortex_m4f_hard \
 *     --config Release --target Foundation
 * @endcode
 *
 * @section FoundationWorkflowBuildPowerShell PowerShell
 *
 * @code{powershell}
 * ./scripts/build.ps1 <preset> [-Configuration <name>] [-Target <name>] `
 *     [-Parallel <jobs>] [-CleanFirst] [-Fresh] [-ExamplesOn]
 * @endcode
 *
 * @section FoundationWorkflowBuildArguments Arguments and Defaults
 *
 * | Argument | Default | Meaning |
 * | --- | --- | --- |
 * | configuration | `Debug` | Selects `Debug` or `Release` in the shared tree. |
 * | target | generator default | Builds one named CMake target when supplied. |
 * | parallel | CMake default | Forwards the requested worker count. |
 * | clean first | off | Cleans the selected configuration before compiling. |
 * | fresh | off | Reconfigures with a fresh CMake cache before building. |
 * | examples | off | Enables repository example targets for this build. |
 *
 * `--target Foundation` is recommended when validating or exporting the library
 * alone. Omitting it builds the generator's default target, which may include
 * examples or tests enabled by earlier cache state.
 *
 * Target presets are configuration-independent. Build defaults to `Debug`; use
 * the explicit option to select `Release`. Both configurations use the same
 * `build/<preset>` directory while Ninja Multi-Config or the native IDE generator
 * keeps their object files isolated.
 *
 * Foundation archives are written below:
 *
 * @code
 * build/<preset>/artifacts/lib/
 * @endcode
 *
 * Debug builds use the `_d` postfix. Release builds produce `libFoundation.a`
 * on Unix-like systems or the corresponding Foundation static library on Windows.
 * Typical names are:
 *
 * | Target | Debug | Release |
 * | --- | --- | --- |
 * | macOS/Linux/Arm/AVR | `libFoundation_d.a` | `libFoundation.a` |
 * | Windows | `Foundation_d.lib` | `Foundation.lib` |
 *
 * @section FoundationWorkflowBuildExamples Building Examples for Development
 *
 * Examples can be compiled in either configuration inside the build tree. This
 * is the supported way to debug or step through an example; exported packages
 * intentionally contain Release examples only.
 *
 * @code{bash}
 * ./scripts/build.sh macos_arm64 --config Debug \
 *     --target FoundationExamples --examples-on
 * @endcode
 *
 * @code{powershell}
 * ./scripts/build.ps1 windows_msvc_x64 -Configuration Debug `
 *     -Target FoundationExamples -ExamplesOn
 * @endcode
 *
 * @section FoundationWorkflowBuildNotDelivery Build Is Not Export
 *
 * Files under `build/` are temporary implementation artifacts. They are not the
 * supported package layout and may contain generator-specific files. Use
 * @ref Foundation_Workflows_Install to overlay one compiled configuration or
 * @ref Foundation_Workflows_Export to create the complete Debug/Release package.
 *
 * @section FoundationWorkflowBuildFailures Common Failures
 *
 * - “preset not found” means the preset is unavailable on that host or its JSON
 *   was not included by `CMakePresets.json`;
 * - “compiler not found” means the required compiler is not on `PATH` and no
 *   configured toolchain root locates it;
 * - missing `stdint.h` in an Arm build usually means the compiler runtime/Newlib
 *   or configured sysroot is incomplete;
 * - architecture validation failures mean a native preset was used on the wrong
 *   host architecture;
 * - a stale generator/compiler error requires a fresh configure or clean build
 *   directory.
 */
